workedExamples.question_text:
The bar represents one whole divided into four equal parts.
Write the fraction, decimal and percentage for (a) the shaded part and (b) the unshaded part.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[scale=0.8]
\fill[gray!40] (0,0) rectangle (1,1);
\draw[black] (0,0) rectangle (4,1);
\foreach \x in {1,2,3} {\draw[black] (\x,0)--(\x,1);}
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

foundation.question_text:
The shaded bar represents part of one whole.
Write the shaded amount as a fraction, decimal and percentage.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\large},scale=0.8]
\fill[gray!40] (0,0) rectangle (2,1);
\draw (0,0) rectangle (4,1);
\foreach \x in {1,2,3} {\draw (\x,0)--(\x,1);}
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

development.question_text:
A $1$ metre strip is divided into quarters and $3$ quarters are shaded.
Write the shaded length as a fraction of the strip, a decimal and a percentage.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\large},scale=0.85]
\fill[gray!40] (0,0) rectangle (4.5,0.8);
\draw (0,0) rectangle (6,0.8);
\foreach \x in {1.5,3,4.5} {\draw (\x,0)--(\x,0.8);}
\node[below] at (0,-0.15) {$0$};
\node[below] at (6,-0.15) {$1\text{ m}$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]
